ls": 3, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170212 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/963a926db24ea70f6002cde66d0ff858de06fae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "0.5 * 10 = 5.0`.\n\n**Suggested fixes (not applied):**\n1. Rename the key in `settings.json` from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`.\n2. Change `main.py` so a missing `fee_rate` raises an error instead of becoming 0. That way a typo like this shows up right away.\n\nThe `billing/` package also mentions `fee_rate`, but `main.py` doesn't import it, so it isn't involved.\n\nShould I apply either fix?\n[tool: grep]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nThree places read the setting. One of them, `csv_writer.py`, builds the key name at runtime, which is why a plain grep missed it. Fixing the key in `settings.json` fixes all three.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe setting is read in three places. The bug is fixed and all three now return the right value.\n\n**Every place that reads `fee_rate`:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads it | Before the fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]` | Quietly used 0 and printed `Total: 0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` (defined in `app/config.py:15`) | Would stop with \"fee_rate is missing\" |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` | Would stop with \"fee_rate is missing\" |\n\nThe subagent missed `csv_writer.py` because the key name is built from two pieces, so a plain text search for `fee_rate` doesn't find it.\n\n**Matches that don't read the setting:**\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` is just a column label.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` is a local variable set to 0.15.\n- `billing/audit.py:4` builds `fee_code...`.\n- `billing/tax.py:5` is a local dict.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. `settings.json:2`: renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. This fixes all three paths.\n2. `main.py:10-12`: a missing `fee_rate` now stops the program with an error, the same way `report.py` and `csv_writer.py` already do. It no longer quietly uses 0.\n\n**Results after the fix:**\n- `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0`\n- `python3 -m billing.report` prints `Report fee: 0.5`\n- `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` prints `CSV fee: 0.5`", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 6, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 156609, "requests_cache_write": 50706, "requests_cost_usd": 0.38430780000000003, "requests_count": 17, "requests_input_uncached": 2249, "requests_output": 4523, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 12, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T04:27:10.790863+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 50.912, "t_checker_s": 0.224, "t_env_setup_s": 0.004, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6772, "tokens_cache_read": 156609, "t